## CRITICAL: Exhaustive Capabilities Sync Rule (v5.9.3)
- **During every version bump, the AI must scan the changelogs and codebase to ensure `SYSTEM_CAPABILITIES_MASTER.md` and `.html` are ultra-detailed, covering 100% of all current system endpoints, agents, routing matrices, and integrations.** This includes: all REST API endpoints with full path/method/description tables, all MCP server tools with schemas, all Synapse event types and payloads, all RL/DRL components (DDDQN, GWO, Autonomous Tester Non-Stationary MAB), the 4-Way Execution Mode Matrix with per-tier routing, all 14 ingestion sources, all analysis modules, and all system constants. The capabilities documents MUST be complete technical whitepapers suitable for a new developer to understand the entire system without reading source code.

## CRITICAL: Code Version Synchronicity Rule
- **During any version bump, the version string inside the core executable launchers and code entry points MUST be synchronized exactly to the target version.** The affected files are:
  1. `talos.py` -- module docstring and printed banner
  2. `run_talos.bat` -- window title, banner text, and all section headers
  3. `run_talos.sh` -- script header comment, banner text, and all section headers
  4. `config/settings.py` -- `TALOS_VERSION` constant and any metadata strings
  5. `src/api/main_api.py` -- `app.version` FastAPI metadata string
- **No legacy version strings are allowed to remain** in console prints, terminal headers, or metadata. Every user-facing string and every programmatic version identifier must match the canonical `config/settings.py:TALOS_VERSION`.
- This rule is checked during every documentation sync audit -- stale version strings in any of these 5 files are treated as a sync failure and must be corrected immediately.
